`verilator_config
// Waivers that apply ONLY to the per-module lint pass, where each module is
// elaborated on its own with the package.
//
// The whole-design pass (lint-rtl) does NOT use this file, on purpose: there,
// "this parameter has no consumer" is a real finding about the design, and the
// Phase 12 review turned up three genuinely dead parameters that way --
// MEM_TILE_ID, VC_PTR_W and SINK_BOUND -- all now deleted. Keeping the waiver
// global would have hidden them.

// A leaf module elaborated alone reads a handful of the package's parameters
// and no more, so every other parameter in coh_pkg looks dead. That is an
// artefact of the pass, not a property of the design.
lint_off -rule UNUSEDPARAM -file "*coh_pkg.sv"
